# glibc floor test (see glibc.cxx). Print the module's dynamic symbols
# with versions above GLIBC_2.36. The expected output is empty.
#
# Note that objdump is part of binutils, which the toolchain includes.
#

: floor
:
objdump -T $0 | \
  sed -n -e 's/^(.*GLIBC_2\.(3[7-9]|[4-9][0-9]|[1-9][0-9]{2,}).*)$/\1/p'

: large-file
:
: Print the module's references to the i386 functions that report inode
: numbers without large file support (see buildfile). The expected output
: is empty.
:
: Note that the statically linked C++ runtime opens files without large
: file support, which only limits their size.
:
objdump -T $0 | \
  sed -n -e 's/^(.*GLIBC_.* (f?stat|fstatat|lstat|readdir))$/\1/p'
